course: dictionary
lesson: 14676
title: The word prescribed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prescribed has two meanings. The first is about doctors: «The doctor prescribed some cream for my rash.» The doctor told the patient to use the cream and wrote it down. Prescribed is the past tense of prescribe, so it tells us the doctor did this in the past.
explain: The second meaning is more formal. It means set by a rule or an authority, so you must follow it. «Please use the prescribed method.» Try the swap check: "Please use the set method" still makes sense, so you know prescribed means set by a rule here.
explain: Clues tell you which meaning is used. Words like doctor, medicine, dose or rule point to the meaning you need. «Take the medicine as prescribed» means take it exactly the way the doctor said.
fact: Prescribed is the past tense and past participle of prescribe (prescribe, prescribes, prescribed, prescribing).
fact: «Prescribed» means told by a doctor to take a medicine or treatment, and written down.
fact: «Prescribed» can also mean set by a rule or authority, as in «the prescribed books».
fact: Phrases to know: «prescribed medicine», «prescribed dose», «as prescribed».
fact: Prescribed medicine is only for the person it was given to, and only at the prescribed dose.
exercise: «The doctor prescribed a cough medicine for Sam.» What did the doctor do? | Asked Sam to sing a song | Gave Sam a long holiday | *Told Sam to take the medicine and wrote it down | Hid the medicine in a box
exercise: «Please finish the test within the prescribed time.» What does prescribed mean here? | Chosen by the student who likes it most | Very long and boring | Written in pencil | *Set by a rule, as the time you are allowed
exercise: «Ella's medicine was prescribed for her, so her brother should not take it.» Why should her brother not take it? | Because it tastes horrible | Because it is for a dog | Because it is too expensive | *Because it was prescribed for Ella only
test: «Take the tablets as prescribed.» What does as prescribed mean? | Only on a Sunday | *Exactly the way the doctor said | With a glass of juice instead of water | Whenever you feel like it
test: «Use the prescribed method for the experiment.» Which word tells you the method is set by a rule? | For | *Prescribed | Experiment | Method
exam: «The doctor prescribed two spoons of syrup, one each morning.» What did the doctor do? | *Wrote down the medicine and told the patient how to take it | Ate the syrup | Sold the syrup in a shop | Forgot all about it
